# 66. Core Success Criteria

The project should demonstrate that:

1. A patient can create a persistent profile.
2. A patient can describe their current problem by speaking or tapping.
3. The AI can ask complaint-relevant follow-up questions.
4. A structured digital clinical report is produced.
5. A patient can upload/scan a medical document.
6. OCR extracts relevant medical information.
7. Information is added to a chronological medical timeline.
8. A patient can book an appointment.
9. A patient receives an appointment QR.
10. The kiosk can identify the patient and confirm arrival.
11. The patient can update information at the kiosk.
12. Red-flag cases can be highlighted.
13. A doctor can view the patient's structured history.
14. A doctor can view original documents.
15. A doctor can verify/edit the AI summary.
16. The doctor remains responsible for diagnosis and treatment.
17. Patient data is protected by authentication and consent controls.

