# 67. Final Product Definition

MediKiosk should ultimately be understood as:

> **A patient-centric AI healthcare platform that creates a persistent digital health profile, collects current symptoms through voice and touch, intelligently asks follow-up questions, digitizes medical documents, builds a chronological medical history, helps patients find and book appropriate healthcare appointments, enables QR-based hospital check-in, and prepares a physician-ready clinical report for authorized doctors before consultation.**

The most important outcome is not that the system has “AI.”

The outcome is:

```text
Patient information
        ↓
Collected before consultation
        ↓
Structured automatically
        ↓
Previous records organized
        ↓
Current complaint understood
        ↓
Relevant information surfaced
        ↓
Doctor receives prepared history
        ↓
Doctor verifies it
        ↓
Doctor spends more consultation time
on examination, reasoning and treatment
```

That is the product's real value. The original problem statement's intended journey already follows the same fundamental sequence: identify and consent, converse, scan records, summarize and route, then allow physician review and consultation.
